// ar/fishing/index.astro — Arabic fishing hub pillar (AR-2 Phase F batch 6a, resumed).
// Mirrors src/pages/fishing/index.astro. SHAPE B, characterized on `guides` and re-used here
// unchanged: prose inline in the template, no page-content module, no collection read.
//
// The offscreen `<p class="page-summary">` renders (`aria-hidden="false"`), so the phone in it
// is isolated exactly as on the hiking page; the JSON-LD copies stay bare.
//
// SLOT 1 — no probe run; no genuinely new digit-bearing construct. `91`, `40` and `349` are
// bare magnitudes; `~1 hour` / `~15 min` take the word `نحو`; `~30–90` and `~5–10` are en-dash
// ranges, measured reversing, so both are spelled `من … إلى …`; the phone takes <bdi>.
//
// §2.2 — first contact for `Green River`, `Little Hole`, `Moon Lake`, `Wyoming Game and Fish`,
// `Utah Division of Wildlife Resources`; all Latin, none carrying a §3.6 digit separator.
// States are localised: `يوتا`, `وايومنغ` — so `the Utah–Wyoming border` becomes a conjunction
// and loses the en dash rather than keeping a reversing shape.
//
// §3.5 — the English glosses `lake trout (mackinaw)` and `Green River (below dam)` would have
// closed a bracket on a Latin run; both are rewritten as apposition with an em dash.
//
// §4 — every internal target on this page is a registered `ar` route, so all of them switch.
